  "description": "T21-1b: a counted-loop index product (`i * n + k`) whose operands the enclosing loops prove nonnegative is lowered as a plain i64 `mul` guarded by one unsigned compare per operand against 2^26 (exact: the product is then below 2^52), and the invalid case folds into the sign bit the bounds check already rejects (`or` with valid-1). No flag-carrying `mulo`/`bo` pair or xor poison select may appear in the kernel. T22's S5.1.2-correct loop-condition slow edge may convert an unproven parameter lane to double elsewhere in the function; it is not part of this index product.",
